  "no_fault_recipe": "Set T=0 and only N=1..5 in the pinned CFG. Also test replacing the Deliver bound SUBSET inTransit in Age_Channel.tla with SUBSET {b \\in inTransit : b.content.to = rcver}, leaving the universal guard in place. Both explicit engines use W1, fp 0, seed 0. The three largest cells have 150 s Core / 160 s external TLC limits; early memory or enumeration stops are recorded separately.",
  "mutant_recipe": "For both: start from Schedule.tla and append FairSchedule == Init /\\ [][Scheduled]_vars /\\ WF_vars(Scheduled) before the terminator; change only SPECIFICATION Spec to SPECIFICATION FairSchedule in the original CFG. Accuracy replaces the value of OnlyMessagesForCorrectProcesses(msgs) with {}. Completeness replaces the union in the Predict assignment by suspected[i], and uses IF ~failed[Victim] in Scheduled for a crash before the first send. For replay use the corresponding unmodified-schedule root EnvironmentController.tla with the original configuration.",
